{"file":"D:\\tool\\go\\src\\io\\fs\\walk.go","checksum":"09de459e421e28f05c2eae1b5848cc616aa0879760d24e955faa056de47c26f0","lang":"go","pkg":"fs","nodes":[{"ID":"import:errors","Kind":"import","Name":"errors","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":8,"Column":2,"Offset":182},"End":{"Line":8,"Column":10,"Offset":190}},"Exported":false,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"","Receiver":null,"Params":null,"Returns":null,"Fields":null,"Implements":null,"Extends":"","TypeParams":null,"AliasTarget":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"EnumMembers":null,"ImportPath":"errors","ImportAlias":"","ImportNames":null,"ImportAll":false,"TypeHint":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"ValueLiteral":"","Callee":"","CallArgs":null,"RawSource":"","UnknownReason":"","Children":null,"Else":null},{"ID":"import:path","Kind":"import","Name":"path","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":9,"Column":2,"Offset":192},"End":{"Line":9,"Column":8,"Offset":198}},"Exported":false,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"","Receiver":null,"Params":null,"Returns":null,"Fields":null,"Implements":null,"Extends":"","TypeParams":null,"AliasTarget":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"EnumMembers":null,"ImportPath":"path","ImportAlias":"","ImportNames":null,"ImportAll":false,"TypeHint":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"ValueLiteral":"","Callee":"","CallArgs":null,"RawSource":"","UnknownReason":"","Children":null,"Else":null},{"ID":"variable:SkipDir","Kind":"variable","Name":"SkipDir","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":15,"Column":5,"Offset":383},"End":{"Line":15,"Column":48,"Offset":426}},"Exported":true,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"SkipDir is used as a return value from [WalkDirFunc] to indicate that\nthe directory named in the call is to be skipped. It is not returned\nas an error by any function.","Receiver":null,"Params":null,"Returns":null,"Fields":null,"Implements":null,"Extends":"","TypeParams":null,"AliasTarget":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"EnumMembers":null,"ImportPath":"","ImportAlias":"","ImportNames":null,"ImportAll":false,"TypeHint":{"Name":"?","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"ValueLiteral":"errors.New(\"skip this directory\")","Callee":"","CallArgs":null,"RawSource":"","UnknownReason":"","Children":null,"Else":null},{"ID":"variable:SkipAll","Kind":"variable","Name":"SkipAll","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":20,"Column":5,"Offset":614},"End":{"Line":20,"Column":62,"Offset":671}},"Exported":true,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"SkipAll is used as a return value from [WalkDirFunc] to indicate that\nall remaining files and directories are to be skipped. It is not returned\nas an error by any function.","Receiver":null,"Params":null,"Returns":null,"Fields":null,"Implements":null,"Extends":"","TypeParams":null,"AliasTarget":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"EnumMembers":null,"ImportPath":"","ImportAlias":"","ImportNames":null,"ImportAll":false,"TypeHint":{"Name":"?","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"ValueLiteral":"errors.New(\"skip everything and stop the walk\")","Callee":"","CallArgs":null,"RawSource":"","UnknownReason":"","Children":null,"Else":null},{"ID":"type:WalkDirFunc","Kind":"type_alias","Name":"WalkDirFunc","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":69,"Column":6,"Offset":3161},"End":{"Line":69,"Column":64,"Offset":3219}},"Exported":true,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"WalkDirFunc is the type of the function called by [WalkDir] to visit\neach file or directory.\n\nThe path argument contains the argument to [WalkDir] as a prefix.\nThat is, if WalkDir is called with root argument \"dir\" and finds a file\nnamed \"a\" in that directory, the walk function will be called with\nargument \"dir/a\".\n\nThe d argument is the [DirEntry] for the named path.\n\nThe error result returned by the function controls how [WalkDir]\ncontinues. If the function returns the special value [SkipDir], WalkDir\nskips the current directory (path if d.IsDir() is true, otherwise\npath's parent directory). If the function returns the special value\n[SkipAll], WalkDir skips all remaining files and directories. Otherwise,\nif the function returns a non-nil error, WalkDir stops entirely and\nreturns that error.\n\nThe err argument reports an error related to path, signaling that\n[WalkDir] will not walk into that directory. The function can decide how\nto handle that error; as described earlier, returning the error will\ncause WalkDir to stop walking the entire tree.\n\n[WalkDir] calls the function with a non-nil err argument in two cases.\n\nFirst, if the initial [Stat] on the root directory fails, WalkDir\ncalls the function with path set to root, d set to nil, and err set to\nthe error from [fs.Stat].\n\nSecond, if a directory's ReadDir method (see [ReadDirFile]) fails, WalkDir calls the\nfunction with path set to the directory's path, d set to an\n[DirEntry] describing the directory, and err set to the error from\nReadDir. In this second case, the function is called twice with the\npath of the directory: the first call is before the directory read is\nattempted and has err set to nil, giving the function a chance to\nreturn [SkipDir] or [SkipAll] and avoid the ReadDir entirely. The second call\nis after a failed ReadDir and reports the error from ReadDir.\n(If ReadDir succeeds, there is no second call.)\n\nThe differences between WalkDirFunc compared to [path/filepath.WalkFunc] are:\n\n  - The second argument has type [DirEntry] instead of [FileInfo].\n  - The function is called before reading a directory, to allow [SkipDir]\n    or [SkipAll] to bypass the directory read entirely or skip all remaining\n    files and directories respectively.\n  - If a directory read fails, the function is called a second time\n    for that directory to report the error.","Receiver":null,"Params":null,"Returns":null,"Fields":null,"Implements":null,"Extends":"","TypeParams":null,"AliasTarget":{"Name":"func","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":true,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"EnumMembers":null,"ImportPath":"","ImportAlias":"","ImportNames":null,"ImportAll":false,"TypeHint":{"Name":"","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"ValueLiteral":"","Callee":"","CallArgs":null,"RawSource":"","UnknownReason":"","Children":null,"Else":null},{"ID":"func:walkDir","Kind":"function","Name":"walkDir","Language":"go","Span":{"Start":{"Line":72,"Column":1,"Offset":3278},"End":{"Line":103,"Column":2,"Offset":3946}},"Exported":false,"Abstract":false,"Async":false,"Static":false,"DocComment":"walkDir recursively descends path, calling walkDirFn.","Receiver":null,"Params":[{"Name":"fsys","Type":{"Name":"FS","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"Variadic":false,"Optional":false,"Default":""},{"Name":"name","Type":{"Name":"string","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"Variadic":false,"Optional":false,"Default":""},{"Name":"d","Type":{"Name":"DirEntry","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":false,"IsPtr":false,"IsFunc":false,"Params":null,"KeyType":null},"Variadic":false,"Optional":false,"Default":""},{"Name":"walkDirFn","Type":{"Name":"WalkDirFunc","Package":"","IsSlice":false,"IsMap":f